Tou-Hum-Mal-Neu
genocideless, artiwishless, polypileless, artiwishless

My quest to ascend all roles in alphabetical order continues, this
time it is Tourist. My hopes of extending my streak were promptly
crushed few hunderd turns into the first Tourist game, where I got
rolled over by a boulder. Only eighth game took off the ground.

1) Went to Minetown first, then two levels below, but did not proceed
to Mine's End as going without poison resistance and magic resistance
seemed too dangerous.

2) I returned to main dungeon and did Sokoban, I got amulet of
reflection there.

3) I got three bones, the third being wizard. With CoMR, reflection
and poison resistance I did Mine's End.

4) After lot of sacrificing I got crowned, which meant Vorpal Blade. I
wanted to stash the sword, but then I realized I won't be getting any
better weapon, so I unpacked it again and used it for the rest of the
game as my main weapon. It turned out not to be as bad as I expected.
Especially with persistent monsters like demons and master- or arch-
liches the beheading often ended the fight.

5) I got the titan version of Medusa's level. I burnt Elbereth on
upstairs, dropped my oilskin bag and started to fight. The titan
summoned monsters, one of them cockatrice. So I stepped off the stairs
to get its coprse, wielded it and stoned the titan. Unfortunately, the
summoned monster beat me to 24 HP (my AC was -3) and I was confused by
umber hulk. After some deliberation I decided the only workable route
is to break my (only) wand of teleportation, which teleported all
monsters but a sasquatch away. I managed to kill the sasquatch with
some luck.

6) I survived, but the blast of teleportation teleported my bag, too,
with all it's water crossing equipment. With some trepidation I dug
down. Surprisingly, the level below Medusa was not maze, but regular
rooms and corridors level -- even furnished with a lawful temple! I
ascended the stairs and in a single blow my Vorpal Blade decapitated
Medusa! In the statue of Perseus there were levitation boots.

7) I returned to my dlvl 8 stash, made more holy water, created YDSM
-- I needed improve my AC and the yellow scales were the only thing I
had.

8) I cleared the Castle without a hitch and wished for speed boots and
bag of holding.

9) I embarked on quest, which was quite protracted (many rooms to
explore) and contained insane amount of loot. My Vorpal Blade
decapitated Master of Thieves in a single blow.

10) I returned to my dlvl 8 stash and sorted through it, then went to
Castle again. Titan was generated there and it was quite a fight to
kill him.

11) In Valley of the Dead I found second wand of wishing and got two
wraith corpses, boosting me to XL 18. I established my main stash and
did some enchanting. Unfortunately, I realized that my tourist is not
going to spellcast magic mapping. In fact, my tourist never seriously
used any magic - pure combat wombat.

12) I used scrolls of magic mapping at alternating levels for Gehennom
exploration. I killed Vlad with +0 rubber hose called Vladbane (took
16 blows). I killed Orcus with cockatrice corpse to get my only wand
of death. I had rather a shortage of digging wands I relied on, since
I couldn't invoke PYEC often enough.

13) After finding VS and final preparations I was maxHP 262, AC -39
(with +3 ring of protection). I had prepared lik 6 cursed potions of
gain level, too. Main weapons were +6 Vorpal Blade and +7 silver sword
with +6 elven daggers as ranged weapon against mind flayers and like.
All looked fine and dandy.

14) When killing Rodney I had the silly idea to eat Rodney for
teleport control. There was vampire lord around who kept interrupting
me as I devoured the wizard's body, so I ate him in like 4-5 steps.
Each time penalty for eating human was applied. I didn't care for
telepathy or alignment, but the 2-5 luck penalty was something I
should have thought of. The result of this was, that my luck went to
deeply negative value.

15) The first indication of problems was, when I couldn't find non-
random secret door at Sanctum graveyard. After many turns searching I
just blasted through. The Sanctum was overall very easy and I bailed
out with c!oGL.

16) The way up was unusually swift and last levels of Gehennom I just
quaffed the c!oGLs I had. I reached the Planes with 3 Rodney
visitations.

17) Plane of Earth was nominal, Plane of Air was very swift as was
Fire. For the Plane of Water I donned oilsking cloak and levitation
boots to play it safe.

18) On the Astral Plane I wanted to wish for the usual trice corpse,
but here my mistake at Rodney's Tower got back at me: "Unfortunately,
nothing happens." This was cold shower indeed, as I had 6+2 wishes
left. Anyway I tried again and this time I got my trice. After that,
it was quick run to the first altar, which turned to be the right one
and guarded only by Famine. The final game dump shows that I ended
with luck -2.

Next goes dwarven lawful female Valkyrie.


